# Don't build or test

Never run a build, test, or verification command on your own initiative:

- `xcodebuild`, `swift build`, `swift test`, Xcode, simulators
- `npm run build`, `npm test`, and equivalents in other toolchains
- Any long-running compile, test-suite, or CI-style command

Make the changes and stop. State what you changed and let Alexis run it himself.

Writing or editing test code is fine when the task calls for it. Running it is not.

Only run these when he explicitly asks ("build it", "run the tests", "verify this
compiles"), or when a plan he approved lists verification as a step.
